description:
Digital lending platform Moneyview&rsquo;s IPO saw strong investor demand, with the issue subscribed 98.5X on the final day of bidding. Qualified institutional buyers (QIBs) led the demand, with their portion subscribed over 227X.
Moneyview&rsquo;s initial public offering (IPO) was open for subscription from September 24-September 28, with a price band of Rs 32-34 and a minimum investment of Rs 14,112 for a lot size of 441 shares.&nbsp;
